# Run the app on port 3035

The app must stay running on **port 3035** (already configured in `package.json`:
`dev` and `start` both use `--port 3035`).

## When the server is down
Build and start it:

```bash
npm run build && npm run start
```

## After finishing any code change
Always rebuild and restart so the running app reflects the latest code:

```bash
# free the port if something is already bound to it
lsof -ti:3035 | xargs kill -9 2>/dev/null || true
npm run build && npm run start
```

## Notes
- Use `npm run start` (production) for the persistent instance; use `npm run dev`
  only for active local iteration.
- Run the server as a background process so it keeps serving.
- Quick health check: `curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://localhost:3035/`
